te. Concerns: arrogance, hot temper, moody, loner, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate to recommend now. Let's weigh: C has reliability, crew atmosphere positive, quick correct decisions, calm, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. B has reliability, stress, technical, but weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks. D has problem solving, responsibility, but arrogance and hot temper, which affect crew cooperation and stress. A has anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but unfriendly, unhealthy, show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich is best overall? C's strengths are strong on reliability, crew atmosphere, decision, calm. Concerns are communication and egocentric, not willing to further education. Those are important but perhaps less safety-critical than memory weakness (B) or arrogance/hot temper (D). Communication difficulty could affect safety, but if he puts concern for others above everything, maybe mitigates? Egocentric may affect teamwork. Not willing to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nThus C still seems strongest. D's arrogance and hot temper are serious for crew cooperation, which is safety-critical. So I will keep recommendation for Candidate C, but note D's strengths and concerns.\n\nWe should reference Agent 1's answer about D's stress handling and crew cooperation, and compare to C's strengths. Also reference Agent 2's memory weakness for B. So we can say we remain with C.\n\nThus produce public message: I agree with Agent 2's shift to C, because D's stress handling is adequate but his arrogance and hot temper undermine crew cooperation, making him less suitable than C, whose reliability and positive crew atmosphere outweigh communication issues.\n\nVote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
